.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/strip-json-comments Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "strip-json-comments [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.com/sindresorhus/strip-json-comments.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.com/github/sindresorhus/strip-json-comments)"
.PP
.RS 4
Strip comments from JSON\&. Lets you use comments in your JSON files! 
.RE
.PP

.PP
This is now possible:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
    // Rainbows
    "unicorn": /* ❤ */ "cake"
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
It will replace single-line comments \fR//\fP and multi-line comments \fR/**/\fP with whitespace\&. This allows JSON error positions to remain as close as possible to the original source\&.

.PP
Also available as a \fRGulp\fP/\fRGrunt\fP/\fRBroccoli\fP plugin\&.
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install strip\-json\-comments
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const json = `{
    // Rainbows
    "unicorn": /* ❤ */ "cake"
}`;

JSON\&.parse(stripJsonComments(json));
//=> {unicorn: 'cake'}
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "stripJsonComments(jsonString, options?)"
.SS "jsonString"
Type: \fRstring\fP

.PP
Accepts a string with JSON and returns a string without comments\&.
.SS "options"
Type: \fRobject\fP
.SS "whitespace"
Type: \fRboolean\fP\\ Default: \fRtrue\fP

.PP
Replace comments with whitespace instead of stripping them entirely\&.
.SH "Benchmark"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm run bench
.fi
.PP
